Step 1 — Create the experiment files
In GitHub, open your Generative-AI-Laboratory repository and select Add file → Create new file.

Create these files inside Experiment-04-MNIST-VAE/ and paste the corresponding code.
Step 2 — Set up Python
On your computer, open the experiment folder in VS Code.

Create a virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv



Activate it on Windows PowerShell:

.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1



Step 3 — Install dependencies

python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt



Step 4 — Run the VAE

python vae.py



The first run downloads MNIST if it is not already cached. The model trains for 10 epochs and saves the generated images and model files.
Step 5 — Verify results
Check that the outputs/ directory contains all three PNG images. Open them to inspect reconstruction quality, generated digit images, and the training loss curves.

The generated digits may look blurry or ambiguous after only 10 epochs. This is normal for a small VAE with a two-dimensional latent space.
